$string['videourl'] = 'Bunny Stream video';
$string['videourl_help'] = 'Paste the Bunny Stream video ID (the "Video ID" in the Bunny dashboard, formatted 8-4-4-4-12, e.g. 1a2b3c4d-5e6f-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d) or any of the links Bunny gives you: the player link (player.mediadelivery.net/play/... or iframe.mediadelivery.net/embed/...) or the playlist link (https://.../playlist.m3u8). Only the ID is stored.

If you fill in this field and the Vimeo one, the Bunny video plays. That way a video can be migrated without deleting the Vimeo one, and emptying this field switches back to Vimeo.

Bunny Stream must be configured in the plugin settings for this to play. Until it is, the activity keeps using the Vimeo video.

The video must be in the site\'s Bunny library. Once Bunny is configured, the form rejects links from another library or another server.

As the cover image, the player always shows the thumbnail Bunny generates from the video (thumbnail.jpg). A custom thumbnail uploaded in Bunny gets a different file name and is not shown.';
